1. DEFINITIONS

"Toolkit" means FDK itself: its source code, object code, headers,
build scripts, build configuration, documentation, the command-line
tools shipped with it (fdk-theme, fdk-set, fdk-prefs), and the
toolkit assets it ships (including the bundled .fdk theme faces), in
whole or in part, in original or modified form.

"Application" means software created by a developer that uses or links
against the Toolkit. An Application includes that developer's own
source code, object code, assets, resources, and branding. An
Application does NOT include the Toolkit itself, any modified version
of the Toolkit, or any part of the Toolkit.

"Runtime Copy" means a binary form of the Toolkit that an Application
needs to be present at run time in order to execute — for example,
the FDK shared library (libfdk) installed on an end user's system. A
Runtime Copy is and remains part of the Toolkit, not part of an
Application, wherever it is installed, however it is obtained, and
whoever installs it.

"Licensor" means FemBoyGamerTechGuy, the copyright holder of the
Toolkit, identified here by the established project handle under
which the Toolkit is authored and published.

"You" means any individual or entity that obtains access to the
Toolkit, in any form and through any channel.

"Written Authorization" means an express, written permission issued
by the Licensor for a specific act or set of acts. This license
itself is one such authorization, for the acts it expressly permits.

