4. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to the terms of this license, the Licensor grants You a
limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

  a. Download, install, and use the Toolkit, and to make the copies
     of it (including backup copies) that are reasonably necessary to
     do so, for the purpose of developing, building, testing, and
     running Applications;

  b. Build Applications that link against, bind, or otherwise
     incorporate the Toolkit;

  c. Distribute and commercially sell or otherwise exploit Your
     Applications, subject to Section 5; and

  d. Rely on a separately installed FDK runtime. An Application You
     distribute must consist of Your own code, assets, and
     branding. You may NOT bundle, embed, statically link,
     redistribute, or otherwise package or include the Toolkit — or
     any Runtime Copy of it — in or with anything You distribute:
     not in or with the Application itself, its installer, a
     container or sandbox image, an archive, or any other
     distribution artifact, unless the Licensor first grants that
     permission in a further, specific Written Authorization. The
     FDK runtime is obtained and installed separately by the end
     user, from the Licensor or from a channel the Licensor
     authorizes. Stating that Your Application requires the FDK
     runtime, or directing users to an authorized channel for it,
     is permitted and does not constitute distributing the Toolkit.

5. APPLICATIONS AND DEVELOPER RIGHTS

  a. Applications are independent works. To the maximum extent
     permitted by applicable law, this license claims no rights over
     Applications, and the Licensor neither owns nor co-owns an
     Application by virtue of its author having used the Toolkit to
     build it.

  b. You retain all rights in and to Your Applications, including
     their source code, assets, branding, and licensing. You may
     distribute, license, sell, or otherwise exploit Your
     Applications under terms You choose, subject to applicable law,
     to any separate agreements that bind You, and to the licenses of
     third-party components You include in them.

  c. Applications do not become the property of the Licensor or of
     the Faded Dream Project merely because they use FDK. The
     restrictions of Section 6 attach to the Toolkit, never to
     independent Application code or assets.

  d. Nothing in this license limits Your right to state factually
     that Your Application is built with FDK. However, You may not
     name, brand, or market Your Application in a way that states or
     implies that it IS the Toolkit, that it is part of the Faded
     Dream Project, or that the Licensor endorses it, without prior
     Written Authorization.

  e. The boundary: if You extract, adapt, or republish Toolkit code,
     Toolkit components, or Toolkit assets outside of an Application
     — for example, as another toolkit, framework, library, template,
     or asset collection — that act is governed by Section 6, not by
     this Section.

  f. The separate-runtime rule in Section 4(d) is a limit on what
     You may distribute of the Toolkit, never on Your Application.
     An Application that requires a separately installed FDK runtime
     is none the less complete, independent, and fully distributable
     under this Section, and nothing in that rule restricts Your
     Application's own packaging, installer, pricing, distribution
     channels, or terms — so long as the artifact You distribute
     does not itself contain or accompany the Toolkit or a Runtime
     Copy of it.

